267
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,160
It waffles!

268
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:46,640
I'm better now!

269
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,860
How did you punch that thing?

270
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,592
I thought everything here was a hologram.

271
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:54,600
Still curious? Then listen closely.

272
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:59,331
With these light pressure gloves, I can
do more than just observe holograms.

273
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:02,130
Hi!

274
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,068
What happens when someone
touches an object?

275
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:08,157
They perceive it as real, don't they?

276
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,040
So she's not real? No way!

277
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:11,500
Shall we find out?

278
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,320
Loopy, watch out!

279
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:22,300
She wasn't real after all.

280
00:15:22,420 --> 00:15:25,297
I don't know what can't kill
me and what can't anymore.

281
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:26,717
What decides if she's real?

282
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:30,400
If anything is, that's for
you to determine on your own.

283
00:15:30,740 --> 00:15:32,957
Rigid thinking needs to
become a thing of the past.

284
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,120
That's what I say.

285
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,440
Stop ignoring me!

286
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:40,739
Perhaps I should have asked
sooner, but who are you?

287
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:43,250
Me?

288
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:47,060
Hey, nothing but a humble
genius scientist for hire!

289
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,360
Doctor Vegapunk!

290
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:04,780
Doctor Vegapunk?

291
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:06,500
Kobe told me about you!

292
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,327
How come you're a giant kid?

293
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:11,420
What the hell is this liar talking about?

294
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:20,797
So what's our next move
here's what we know?

295
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,617
There's only one man with
a mind like Vegapunks.

296
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:28,117
And a genius like that always has a
full plate of course—he could use some

297
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:31,777
help with his work—but no one else
can keep up with that thought in mind.

298
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:35,537
He had an idea: what if he split
himself into six different people?

299
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:37,717
Those offshoots are called satellites.

300
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:40,717
The satellites function as.

301
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,697
function as their own individuals.

302
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:45,620
But at the end of the
day, they're all Vegapunk.

303
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:47,214
If you weren't the one

304
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:52,177
telling me, I'd say this
was too insane to be true.

305
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:53,517
Six geniuses.

306
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:54,697
This'll be a pain.

307
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,660
So we make our way to Egghead.

308
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:58,797
We tell them we're returning this.

309
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:01,740
And once we're in, we
kill all of the Vegapunks.

310
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,737
Yes, but his lab's full
of priceless research.

311
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:07,637
Let's try to keep the
damage to a They want us

312
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:10,426
to eliminate the most
useful man in the world.

313
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:13,211
Does this have something to do with Lucia?

314
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,424
Considering the timing it must.

315
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:17,700
Lucci, you're a smart boy.

316
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:21,237
You should know better than
to be nosy about these things.

317
00:17:21,320 --> 00:17:22,555
Listen to her, Lucci.

318
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:25,157
Trouble for you means
trouble for all of us.

319
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,070
Let it go.

320
00:17:27,820 --> 00:17:28,650
Uh-huh.

321
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,240
It was so good.

322
00:17:30,520 --> 00:17:32,540
Too bad everyone else missed out.

323
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,257
Guess we'll have to eat again.

324
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:36,177
I can't wait to show
them the food machine.

325
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,460
They're gonna love it for sure.

326
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:41,220
Well, Sanji might not be too happy.

327
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:43,080
You sure made a big mess.

328
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:46,057
And those bellies, they look
like they're about to burst.

329
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:47,780
I always look like this.

330
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,320
Gotta work, buddy.

331
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,360
Wait, what's your job?

332
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,537
Oh, you know, just violence and stuff.

333
00:18:00,620 --> 00:18:01,680
I'm sorry, what?

334
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,180
Are those robots too?

335
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:22,600
This place is a lab, isn't it?

336
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:24,757
My guess is that they're researchers.

337
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:28,517
There wasn't anyone in town at
first, but now there's a whole crowd.

338
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,430
How odd.

339
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:32,377
Perhaps they were waiting
to see if we posed a threat.

340
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:34,107
Their clothes look so heavy.

341
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:36,297
Aren't they too hot in this weather?

342
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:37,977
Wait a second.

343
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:39,260
Where'd Luffy go?

344
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,802
That sounded like Luffy's voice.

345
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,220
What are you doing?

346
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,816
And then I tap back!

347
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:49,950
Luffy!

348
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:51,840
What's he doing in there?

349
00:18:54,620 --> 00:18:55,720
Hey, guys!

350
00:18:56,160 --> 00:18:57,219
What do you think?

351
00:18:57,480 --> 00:18:58,600
Do you like it?

352
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:04,797
I love how this feels.

353
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:07,100
It looks kind of heavy.

354
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,900
It's actually not at all.

355
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:10,720
And it's cool inside.

356
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:13,220
You look quite nice.

357
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:14,900
I want one.

358
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:16,797
You got the clothes in there?

359
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:17,980
Yeah, going in.

360
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:20,000
Free food and free clothes?

361
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,380
The future is so handy.

362
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,577
I do feel a little sticky
thanks to that seawater.

363
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:26,490
Welcome.

364
00:19:26,573 --> 00:19:28,817
Please choose your
preferred clothing style.

365
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:30,360
In that case...

366
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:32,780
Come back here.

367
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:39,960
I can quite dress myself, okay? Wow!

368
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,580
He was right.

369
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,317
I'm as light as a feather.

370
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,753
I feel like I'm floating in these shoes.

371
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,020
This is great.

372
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:54,130
The future.

373
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:58,040
I'm glad they had something
tropical, too. Oh, yeah.

374
00:19:58,300 --> 00:20:00,580
It was amazing, G-Babe. Thank you.

375
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:03,036
Hopefully this will help us blend in.

376
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:05,773
Although, it might be too late for that.

377
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:08,697
I'm going to go and look for a weapon.

378
00:20:08,780 --> 00:20:10,317
Then I'm going to try to find Vegapunk.

379
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:11,230
So I'm off.

380
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:12,402
See you around.

381
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:14,287
Stay safe out there, Bonnie!

382
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,020
Yeah, good luck!

383
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:25,610
Wait!

384
00:20:30,460 --> 00:20:32,080
It's Kuma. Really?

385
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:34,213
He could be in trouble.

386
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:35,575
Is he looking for us?

387
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:41,060
Let's go! Huh?

388
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:44,420
Gotta run for it, guys!

389
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,677
He's definitely coming for us!

390
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:47,590
Wait!

391
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:54,297
Can you tell me who we're
running away from and why?

392
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,210
Later, okay?

393
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:57,940
Damn it, no!

394
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:10,135
Aggravated theft of food and clothing.

395
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:15,000
Watch out!

396
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:16,121
He's gonna fire!

397
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:25,500
It didn't ask for money!

398
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:26,857
It worked when I hit it!

399
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:28,881
That sounds like vandalism to me!

400
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,040
This is crazy!

401
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:37,477
He's trying to kill us!

402
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:39,207
The law here is quite harsh.

403
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:45,277
Looks like he's going all out!

404
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:46,457
We gotta fight back!

405
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:50,860
Yes, we may be pirates, but
self-defense is self-defense. Let's go!

406
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,300
I'm sorry, Kuma!

407
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:14,680
All right, Kuma Kuma!

408
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:24,000
Stop it!

409
00:22:34,340 --> 00:22:36,020
What's your deal, Bonnie?

410
00:22:36,280 --> 00:22:38,140
He's using lasers on us.

411
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:39,880
Can I at least hit him?

412
00:22:48,820 --> 00:22:50,380
He's my father.

413
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:56,460
He's all I've got.

414
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:01,560
He's the only family I have.

415
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:11,304
When you said your dad
got turned into a cyborg.

416
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,200
You were talking about Kuma?

417
00:23:31,740 --> 00:23:33,857
This isn't his fault.

418
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,877
So don't hurt my father.

419
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:37,177
I'm begging you.

420
00:23:37,260 --> 00:23:38,577
Run away, you dummy!

421
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:40,480
That's a pacifista? Stop!

422
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:45,090
Bonnie!

423
00:23:45,180 --> 00:23:46,010
Bonnie!

424
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:05,200
Close valve two, quick!

425
00:24:06,260 --> 00:24:07,460
We need cover here!

426
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:09,340
Here, Duke!

427
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:13,860
I see something dead ahead!

428
00:24:14,080 --> 00:24:15,140
Turn now!

429
00:24:20,940 --> 00:24:22,440
It's no use, Captain!

430
00:24:22,740 --> 00:24:23,800
We can't escape!

431
00:24:36,340 --> 00:24:38,080
Come out and bite me!

432
00:24:48,260 --> 00:24:49,920
We can't take another hit.

433
00:24:50,100 --> 00:24:51,977
The water pressure's
going to crush the sub.

434
00:24:52,060 --> 00:24:54,236
Captain, you've got to make the call.

435
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:00,320
Let's surface.

436
00:25:01,140 --> 00:25:02,900
To the northeast, near land.

437
00:25:03,620 --> 00:25:04,660
Fire, Captain.

438
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:06,840
We're headed for land.

439
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:08,760
Forward to starboard.

440
00:25:15,540 --> 00:25:17,187
Everyone get ready to fight!

441
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:18,150
Let's go!

442
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:22,670
Damn it.

443
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:24,407
Must be a Devil Fruit power.

444
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:26,820
We're in their trap. Be careful!

445
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:28,340
Aye, aye, cutie.

446
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:29,421
I mean, captain.

447
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:32,408
If you don't shut your
mouths, I'll gut you!

448
00:25:32,780 --> 00:25:34,721
You're cute when you're mad, too!

449
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:37,500
Oh, no!

450
00:25:37,840 --> 00:25:39,200
I've been glorified!

451
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:41,630
Ah!

452
00:25:41,713 --> 00:25:43,200
It's spreading to the entire crew!

453
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:46,840
Then stay away from the
infected! Oops. Sorry.

454
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:49,800
It's functioning like
a contagious disease.

455
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:51,845
How are they changing our sex?

456
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:53,070
Woo-hoo!

457
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:54,840
Never mind.

458
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:57,993
I learned something fighting an emperor.

459
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:00,340
I can break through this!

460
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:02,520
You intensify your Haki!

461
00:26:02,940 --> 00:26:04,880
It nullifies devil-proof powers!

462
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:22,419
We've reached the surface, Captain!

463
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:24,400
I'm okay!

464
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:27,840
I did it.

465
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:30,120
There's no power you can't beat!

466
00:26:30,580 --> 00:26:32,677
We can celebrate when
we've won this fight.

467
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:33,760
Doc the sub.

468
00:26:33,940 --> 00:26:35,058
We're going ashore.

469
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:36,220
Aye, aye, sir!

470
00:26:42,300 --> 00:26:44,860
Seems he cured the disease already.

471
00:26:45,460 --> 00:26:49,340
He's worth three billion for a
reason, I suppose. Andy Twig.

472
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:51,497
As soon as he broke through the illness,

473
00:26:51,580 --> 00:26:54,521
his antibodies spread as
quickly as the contagion.

474
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:57,860
But it was fun while it lasted.

475
00:26:58,180 --> 00:26:59,592
My feminization disease.

476
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:04,310
Hmm.

477
00:27:04,393 --> 00:27:06,840
Burgess, I'll move us to the island.

478
00:27:09,320 --> 00:27:10,400
Hell yeah!

479
00:27:20,700 --> 00:27:23,900
Guys, is that mountain moving? No!

480
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:26,005
There's someone lifting it up!

481
00:27:39,100 --> 00:27:42,780
this is true power thanks
to the strong strong fruit

482
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:50,737
so what he can just toss around
whole mountains now and how

483
00:27:50,820 --> 00:27:54,097
did he manage to get to the
shore so quickly they're using

484
00:27:54,180 --> 00:27:58,977
Devil Fruit powers teleportation
contagion superhuman strength

485
00:27:59,060 --> 00:28:02,597
They must have gained these by
hunting for specific abilities.

486
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:04,974
I see where their bounties keep rising.

487
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:17,420
Now, roam.

488
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:25,390
Amputate!

489
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:58,497
It's been a while, hasn't it?

490
00:28:58,580 --> 00:28:59,880
Trafalgar Law!

491
00:29:00,700 --> 00:29:02,200
What is this, Blackbeard?

492
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:03,897
What do you want from us?

493
00:29:03,980 --> 00:29:05,160
Don't be so cold!

494
00:29:05,460 --> 00:29:08,284
We're both from the worst
generation, aren't we?

495
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:13,870
Commodore!

496
00:29:15,200 --> 00:29:17,376
Stronger says you're a bit too heavy!

497
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,070
And I agree!

498
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:27,017
I knew someone would be
coming through here from Wano.

499
00:29:27,100 --> 00:29:32,041
I wasn't sure if it would be you, Straw
Hat, or Kid, but that's fine, I'm not picky.

500
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:35,420
I can't believe you took
out Kaido and Big Bob.

501
00:29:35,700 --> 00:29:38,040
You turned the whole world upside down.

502
00:29:38,260 --> 00:29:39,880
Feels good, don't it?

503
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:47,300
I bet you've got a fine
treasure from Kaido, right?

504
00:29:49,140 --> 00:29:51,860
How many rote ponoclyphs do you have now?

505
00:29:52,180 --> 00:29:56,180
I can't wait to find out,
because soon they'll all be mine.

506
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:01,500
I could say the same to you!

507
00:30:07,600 --> 00:30:09,500
So let's do this!

508
00:30:09,940 --> 00:30:11,720
Winner takes all!

509
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:41,517
Thank

510
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:42,917
you

511
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:50,000
so

512
00:30:54,380 --> 00:30:57,060
much for watching.

513
00:31:17,160 --> 00:31:19,877
Thank you

514
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:26,960
very

515
00:31:27,080 --> 00:31:27,910
much.
